@id     01_hello
@title  Hello, C
@topic  output
@lang   c

@theory
Every C program starts running in main(). To print text, use printf from <stdio.h>.

    #include <stdio.h>

    int main(void) {
        printf("Hi!\n");
        return 0;
    }

"\n" moves to a new line. return 0 tells the system the program finished without errors.

Your task: print exactly two lines:
Hello, CodeLens!
I am learning C.

@starter
#include <stdio.h>

int main(void) {
    // print the two lines here

    return 0;
}

@solution
#include <stdio.h>

int main(void) {
    printf("Hello, CodeLens!\n");
    printf("I am learning C.\n");
    return 0;
}

@test
@expected
Hello, CodeLens!
I am learning C.
